{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrRLyxd8b4gJz5kyyTaY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't see the defect itself. The relational `UserMapper` body is elided in the snippets, so this diagnosis is inferred and the line numbers are approximate.\n\nEvery other layer I could see handles `lastName` correctly. That includes the DTOs, `AuthService.validateSocialLogin`, the document mapper's `toPersistence` and `toDomain`, and both entity definitions. Registration and profile updates both go through the users service and then the persistence mapper. The only way a correct `lastName` ends up equal to `firstName` in both flows is a bad field copy in the relational mapper, which is the only mapper whose body I couldn't see."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":10125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71c6b9c0-8a4b-4f65-85a6-f609e26cb1bf","uuid":"56093e21-f621-4a22-8fd5-e4c20f8523a3","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:38:20.478Z","request_id":"req_011CgrRLynD9pBhC4Lg81byn"}
